//RS /// c109 Phase 21 + D-COROUTINE1=A / D-TUPLE-DESTRUCT1: is `(method, nargs)` a
//RS /// Task/Receiver/Sender concurrency method (`emit_builtin_method`'s `Type::Apply`-
//RS /// receiver arms)? `Task.join()/detach()/pause()/pause(mode)/resume()/cancel()`,
//RS /// `Receiver.receive()`, `Sender.send(v)`, `close()`. Card #1685 moved the spawn
//RS /// surface to one keyword with nested combinators, retiring `Task.wait()`,
//RS /// `.trace()`, `.exception()` and the `*_all` task-group twins from this set;
//RS /// `wait`/0 now belongs to `Process` and `trace`/0 to the Event family, both keyed
//RS /// on receiver type below. The arg count disambiguates `Task.join()` (0 args) from
//RS /// the list `join(sep)` (1 arg, shape d) and `Sender.send(v)`
//RS /// (1 arg) — every name+arity here is disjoint from every other covered shape.
