//RS /// Is `method` (with `nargs` args) a numeric method the TIR lowers?
//RS /// This is the D-INTBIG1/D-NUMOPS1 slice of
//RS /// `emit_builtin_method` keyed on a numeric receiver (`recv_type == Some(numeric)`):
//RS /// the float predicates (`is_nan`/`is_infinite`/`is_finite`), the integer bit-pop
//RS /// queries (`count_ones`/`count_zeros`/`leading_zeros`/`trailing_zeros`), and the
//RS /// fixed-width overflow-policy methods. `to_string` on a numeric receiver is NOT here — it sets
//RS /// `recv_type == Some(numeric)` too, but the AST routes it through the plain
//RS /// `to_string` arm (`(recv).jet_show()`), which is the Phase-9 `BuiltinMethod` shape;
//RS /// a numeric `to_string` carries `recv_type == Some`, so it never reaches the Phase-9
//RS /// `recv_type.is_none()` gate — it must be covered here as a distinct op.
